.TH ECHO-AI 1 "September 2026" "echo-ai 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
echo-ai \- agentic AI assistant with a web UI, terminal UI, and tool access
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B echo-ai
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B echo-ai
is an agentic AI assistant: a conversation loop over an LLM provider
(Ollama, OpenAI-compatible endpoints, OpenCode Zen/Go, or Codex) with
access to workspace tools (file read/write/edit, shell, git, web search
and fetch, notes, memory, SQLite, and a browser).
.PP
Two frontends exist: the web server (default, \fB--web\fR) serving a
chat UI over HTTPS with a WebSocket protocol, and a terminal UI
(\fB--cli\fR) built with ratatui.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-web
Run the web server (default).
.TP
.BR \-\-cli
Run the terminal UI.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Load configuration from \fIPATH\fR. Defaults are used when the file
does not exist unless an explicit path was given.
.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Enable debug logging (JSON lines on stderr).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is TOML; the default location is \fBconfig.toml\fR next to
the binary. See \fBconfig.toml.example\fR for all options. Notable
sections:
.TP
.B [agent]
provider, model, temperature, max_iterations, effort.
.TP
.B [server]
port (8443), bind (127.0.0.1), tls (true), optional custom
tls_cert/tls_key.
.TP
.B [safety]
mode, workspace pinning, blocklists, allow_network,
web_fetch_max_chars.
.TP
.B [session]
enabled; the data directory is \fB~/.config/echo-ai\fR
(C-compatible layout: vault files, TLS keys, session database).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/echo-ai/
Vault (\fBsalt\fR, \fB.pepper\fR, \fB.verifier\fR), session database
(\fBecho-ai.db\fR), and generated TLS material (\fBtls/\fR, mode 0600).
.TP
.B ~/.config/echo-ai/notes/
Personal markdown notes (the \fBnotes\fR tool).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ECHO_AI_PASSWORD
Unlock password for the session vault (headless setup).
.TP
.B ECHO_AI_DATA_DIR
Override the data directory.
.TP
.B ECHO_AI_FRONTEND
Override the frontend static files directory.
.TP
.B ECHO_AI_BROWSER
Browser binary for the browser tools (default: chromium).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; nonzero on configuration or server errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project documentation under
.B docs/
(plans, reviews, verification evidence).